  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA passing trough will provide some rain showers for some areas\ntoday. However, any rainfall amounts will be on the lower side.\n\nDry weather can then be expected for Monday night through\nTuesday night. \n\nA cold front will push through the area Wednesday night into \nThursday, bringing widespread precipitation. Some models are \nshowing a few bullseyes over an inch and a half, but most of the\nregion should receive much lower amounts. Models are in much\nbetter agreement with the timing of the system, but still vary\nconsiderably in precipitation amounts. Despite some decent shear\nand low level helicity values, small CAPE values should prevent\nstrong storms, although a rumble of thunder is possible. \n\nA broad upper level parent trough swings through the area later\nFriday into Saturday, possibly providing some showers. Much \ncooler air will move in behind the front for the weekend.",
